Alembic migrations for the Rampart backend (PostgreSQL).

Deploy time
-----------
The backend image runs `python -m api.migrate` from docker-entrypoint.sh before
uvicorn starts, so every `docker-compose up` / ECS task start brings the schema
to head. It is idempotent, serialised with a Postgres advisory lock, and aborts
startup if a migration fails. Set SKIP_DB_MIGRATE=1 to opt out.

Databases created by the legacy api.db.init_*_table() DDL (no alembic_version
table yet) are detected and stamped at the baseline revision automatically; no
manual `alembic stamp` is needed.

Manual use (from backend/, with DATABASE_URL set)
-------------------------------------------------
    python -m api.migrate            # upgrade to head
    python -m api.migrate --check    # exit 1 if behind head
    alembic revision --autogenerate -m "describe change"
    alembic current / history / downgrade -1

SQLite (local dev and the test suite) is created by api.db.init_all_tables() /
create_all_tables(); the baseline revision also applies cleanly to SQLite.
